            "review_text": "阿俊\nBeijing, China3 contributions\n0\nThe Real Experience of Trying Roast Duck Rice in an Exotic Country\nMar 2025 • Solo\nI tried this roast duck rice abroad and it felt very special. The duck is crisp and tender on the outside and tastes delicious, but not overly greasy. The rice was soft and sticky, very comfortable to eat and served well with duck. To be honest, I was a little worried at first and thought it might not be easy to get authentic roast duck rice abroad. But after a bite, I was really surprised that the taste was closer to home than I thought. It's still a little different, but it's satisfying to find such close tastes in a foreign country.\nRead more\nTranslated from Chinese\nShow original\nWritten March 13, 2025",
